    "result_text": "The full build succeeds. Implementation complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a daily registration limit that rejects owner creation with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100+ owners already have today's `registrationDate`, following the existing per-city-capacity pattern:\n\n- **`EnsureDailyLimit`** (`function/owner/`) \u2014 counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals the server's current date and throws `DailyLimitExceededException` at `MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY = 100`. It runs before `BuildOwner`, so an over-limit day is rejected before anything is built or saved.\n- **`DailyLimitExceededException`** \u2014 a checked exception (mirrors `CityCapacityExceededException`).\n- **`DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `429` with the `{\"error\": \"...\"}` body shape used by the sibling handlers.\n- **escalation YAML** mapping the exception to the handler.\n- Wired a new `ensureDailyLimit` step into `owners.POST.yml` between `ensureCityCapacity` and `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\nEach responsibility lives in its own small class, and the today-count reuses `OwnerRepository.findAll()` the same way the other `Ensure*` checks do. The acceptance test (`coreRejectsOverDailyLimit`) and the full suite pass.",
